  "notes": "Source table provides termination rates by years of service only (Male and Female columns). Rates are identical for both genders. Target requires rates by age x service. Since the source defines rates by service only, broadcast is used to repeat the service-based rates across all target ages. Source values are percentages; code will convert to decimal. Target service bins (e.g., 2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12, 30, 40) do not align perfectly with source single-year bins or the '20+' open bin, so overlap_weighted is used to blend rates proportionally to the overlap of the target bin with the source bins. For example, target '2' (service 2) overlaps source '1' (service 1) and '3' (service 3) by 0.5 years each, so the rate is the average of the two. Target '30' and '40' fall entirely within the '20+' source bin, so they copy the '20+' rate.",
  "unavailable": false
